investigators in Florida are trying to  determine how a car rolled off a ferry  into a channel about 50 feet deep  killing both women inside the car was  apparently at the front of the ferry  which was transporting vehicles and  passengers from Fisher Island to Miami  Beach some two miles away Manuel  Bojorquez is in Miami Beach with more on  this story  Manuel I know this is a very popular  route what do they think happen  well good morning it is the Association  which runs the line says it operates  multiple ferries every day now Fisher  Island right over there is billed as one  of the wealthiest communities in the  country with the only ways on or off by  boat or ferry and people who live there  say they have never heard of anything  like this happening before the first  distress calls came in just after 5:00  p.m. Tuesday a Mercedes Benz that was  being driven by 63 year old Emma Afra  with 75 year old Viviane Brahms as her  passenger had somehow rolled off the  ferry dive crews searched the waters  overnight eventually finding the two  deceased women inside the car which was  brought back on shore and towed away  it's still very early in the  investigative process our teams here  from sector Miami alongside Miami Dade  County Police have communicated with the  crew and with passengers and are just  beginning to put those pieces together  the Fisher Island community association  which runs the ferry issued a statement  saying the entire community mourns their  loss and our hearts and prayers go out  to their families and loved ones  this gentleman's I guess putting  something in front of the tire a  producer with Inside Edition took the 7  minute trip on the same ferry line  chalks were put in front of his wheels  to keep the car from rolling they're  reportedly not required by law but the  Coast Guard tells the Miami Herald the  crew is believed to have used them to  secure the Mercedes on Tuesday there was  only what appears to be a thin barrier  of netting between the cars and the  water nobody told me anything about  putting my car in park or turning the  car off Fisher Island is an exclusive  community with a population of about 800  families where the average home costs  more than two million dollars  I've been living  for 23 years and that you know this has  never happened  sources familiar with the investigation  told the Miami Herald Afra may have  forgotten to put the car in park and  then accidentally hit the gas pedal they  also report the women were found in an  apparent embrace in the backseat Anthony  very said Manuel thank you
 

